<title>CANADA: Canam Manac acquires Calgary steel plant.</title>
<headline>Canam Manac acquires Calgary steel plant.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canam Manac Group Inc said on Monday that it had acquired a steel joist fabricating plant in Calgary from Canron Inc, a subsidiary of Ivaco Inc.</p>
<p>Canam said in a statement that the value of the transaction was about C$10 million.</p>
<p>The 46,000 square-foot plant has an annual production capacity of 16,000 tons, Canam said.</p>
<p>Ivaco said in a separate statement that it expects a pre-tax gain of about C$4.6 million from the sale.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
</text>
